&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director of Corporate Development is a senior finance and strategy leader responsible for advancing Oscar&#39;s inorganic growth agenda.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the SVP, Deputy CFO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is based in our Tempe, AZ office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $196,733 - $258,212 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deal Execution: Lead end-to-end corporate development execution across M&amp;amp;A, investments, divestitures, and strategic partnerships, including target sourcing, market mapping, valuation, financial modeling, diligence, negotiation, approval materials, closing, and integration planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration: Partner with operators to define integration plans, synergy/value-capture targets, post-close KPIs, and governance to ensure transactions deliver against strategic and financial objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market mapping: Develop and manage a thesis-driven sourcing strategy that translates enterprise priorities into market landscapes, target universes, build/buy/partner recommendations, and a prioritized pipeline of actionable M&amp;amp;A, investment, and strategic partnership opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Financial and Capital Modeling: Lead sophisticated, long-term, enterprise-wide financial and capital modeling efforts to inform and influence strategic decisions related to future growth initiatives and capital allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Initiative Evaluation &amp;amp; Due Diligence: Provide comprehensive quantitative and qualitative evaluations of strategic growth initiatives, including new market entries and business lines, in close partnership with the Corporate Strategy team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
